    "text": "I read through the minbpe code this session: regex.py, basic.py, base.py, gpt4.py, __init__.py, and the lineage_bench.py harness. The goal was to understand the tokenizer structure and the benchmark before attempting any change.\n\nNothing was measured. I made no edits, ran no sandbox evaluations, and the session ended without a submitted candidate. There are no results to quote.\n\nWhat I believe now is limited to what reading gives me. The code is split into a shared base, a basic tokenizer, a regex-splitting tokenizer, and a GPT-4 compatible wrapper, and the bench script is the thing any change will be judged against. I have not verified where time is actually spent, so any idea about hotspots is untested.\n\nNext session I should not reread everything. I should run lineage_bench.py once on the unmodified code to get a baseline, then pick one concrete change in the training or encoding path, measure it in the sandbox, and submit if it holds up.",
